            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every mile your truck travels puts stress on its engine. While a commercial truck oil change may seem like one of the simplest maintenance tasks, overlooking it or cutting corners can lead to expensive repairs, unnecessary downtime, and a shorter engine lifespan.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators and fleet managers alike, routine maintenance isn't just another item on the calendar. It's one of the smartest investments you can make in your equipment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistake-1",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mistake #1: Waiting Too Long Between Oil Changes",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistake-1"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-1-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every manufacturer recommends a diesel truck maintenance schedule for a reason. Oil gradually loses its ability to lubricate engine components as contaminants, soot, and debris accumulate. Waiting too long between services increases engine wear and can reduce fuel efficiency.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-1-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Factors that may require more frequent service include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-mistake-1-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Frequent stop-and-go driving"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Heavy hauling"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Idling for extended periods"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Dusty job sites"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Extreme temperatures"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-1-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Following a consistent diesel truck maintenance schedule helps protect one of your fleet's biggest investments.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistake-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mistake #2: Ignoring Other Systems During Routine Maintenance",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistake-2"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-2-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "An oil change is one of the best opportunities to inspect other critical truck components. Experienced technicians don't simply drain the oil and send you on your way. They look for early warning signs that could become larger issues later.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-2-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "This includes inspecting:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-mistake-2-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Belts and hoses"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Brake components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Batteries"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Filters"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fluid levels"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tires"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-2-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Routine inspections often identify worn truck cooling system parts before overheating leads to engine damage. Likewise, inspecting diesel fuel system parts helps prevent fuel delivery issues that can affect performance and efficiency. Catching these problems early is far less expensive than roadside repairs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistake-3",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mistake #3: Using Low-Quality Parts",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistake-3"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-3-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not every oil filter or replacement component is built to manufacturer standards. Quality filters help remove contaminants while maintaining proper oil flow throughout the engine. The same is true for replacement cooling system parts and diesel fuel system parts. Choosing genuine or high-quality OEM components helps ensure proper fit, reliable performance, and longer service life.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-mistake-3-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Need Genuine Parts?",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "need-parts-fast"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-3-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Sun State International's online parts store makes it easy to order genuine commercial truck parts backed by trusted manufacturers. Whether you need filters, cooling system components, or replacement fuel system parts, we're here to help keep your trucks moving. Visit the Sun State International Online Parts Store to order genuine truck parts today.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-mistake-3-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-mistake-3-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
