                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/commercial-truck-oil-change-mistakes-that-cost-you/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Diesel oil filter replacement for a commercial truck at Sun State International"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistake-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mistake #4: Treating Every Truck the Same",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistake-4"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-4-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "No two fleets operate exactly alike. A regional delivery truck has different maintenance needs than a long-haul tractor or construction vehicle. Mileage, engine hours, terrain, payload, and operating conditions all affect maintenance intervals. Working with experienced technicians allows you to build a maintenance plan based on how your trucks are actually used instead of relying on a one-size-fits-all schedule. That personalized approach helps improve reliability while reducing unnecessary service costs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistake-5",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Mistake #5: Waiting Until Something Breaks",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistake-5"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-5-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Many expensive engine repairs begin with small issues that could have been caught during preventive maintenance. Leaks, worn filters, contaminated fluids, or failing components rarely happen overnight. Regular inspections and scheduled commercial truck oil change services allow technicians to identify developing problems before they lead to breakdowns. Preventive maintenance is one of the most effective ways to reduce truck downtime services across your fleet.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-5-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Less downtime means:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-mistake-5-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "More deliveries completed"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fewer emergency repairs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Better customer satisfaction"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lower operating costs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Longer equipment life"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-it-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why a Commercial Truck Oil Change Matters More Than You Think",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-it-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Heavy-duty diesel engines operate under extreme conditions every day. Long hauls, stop-and-go traffic, heavy payloads, and Florida's heat all accelerate engine wear. Fresh oil lubricates critical engine components, reduces friction, controls heat, and helps remove contaminants before they damage expensive internal parts. Skipping a scheduled commercial truck oil change doesn't save money. It often creates much larger repair bills later. Preventive maintenance is one of the most effective ways to control those costs while keeping trucks on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/commercial-truck-oil-change-mistakes-that-cost-you/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State International fleet maintenance service for commercial trucks in Florida"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-partner",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Partner With a Service Team That Understands Your Business",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "partner"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-partner-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keeping commercial trucks on the road requires more than changing oil. It requires technicians who understand heavy-duty equipment, access to genuine parts, and a service department committed to your uptime. At Sun State International, we know every hour your truck sits in the shop affects your business. That's why our team focuses on efficient diagnostics, quality repairs, and proactive maintenance designed to keep you moving.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-partner-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Whether you're servicing one truck or an entire fleet, we're here to provide dependable support every step of the way.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-protect",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Protect Your Investment With Preventive Maintenance",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "protect"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-protect-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A routine commercial truck oil change is one of the simplest services you can schedule, but it plays a major role in protecting your engine, reducing repair costs, and extending the life of your truck. Combined with regular inspections, quality truck cooling system parts, reliable diesel fuel system parts, and a customized diesel truck maintenance schedule, preventive maintenance helps keep your fleet productive year-round. If you're looking for trusted service and expert support, Sun State International is ready to help. <a href=\"/service-appointment\">Schedule your next service appointment with Sun State International</a> and keep your trucks operating at their best.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
